WEBVTT

00:21.771 --> 00:24.691
MEETING IN THE RAIN

00:55.764 --> 00:58.475
Coming to me over and over
is a waste of time.

00:58.558 --> 01:01.603
I can't turn you into a Sorcerer.

01:02.145 --> 01:04.981
That book wasn't even about that.

01:06.900 --> 01:08.485
Is that bundle in the back

01:09.194 --> 01:12.447
the body of the Sorcerer
the local association killed?

01:13.782 --> 01:15.617
It's for research.

01:18.203 --> 01:22.123
Plus, it could provide some hints
for treating victims of magic.

01:29.047 --> 01:31.883
These are all Sorcerers?

01:31.966 --> 01:37.514
Yes. I'm secretly collecting the Sorcerers
killed by the local association.

01:38.223 --> 01:40.225
Your name, Kasukabe,

01:41.059 --> 01:42.894
sounds like a Sorcerer's name.

01:43.728 --> 01:46.231
Actually, my wife was a Sorcerer.

01:46.731 --> 01:51.152
When she was ill, I kept thinking
there had to be something I could do.

01:51.236 --> 01:54.405
That's what got me researching Sorcerers.

01:55.198 --> 01:57.200
Your wife was a Sorcerer.

01:57.742 --> 02:00.453
My wife basically abandoned me, though.

02:00.537 --> 02:04.457
When I published my first book,
I used my wife's name.

02:04.541 --> 02:06.668
By the way, what about your family?

02:06.751 --> 02:10.004
Is it okay for you
to be out this late at night?

02:10.630 --> 02:15.176
I have my grandpa, but he's out peddling
and rarely comes home.

02:15.760 --> 02:18.179
Why do you want to become a Sorcerer?

02:18.263 --> 02:19.931
WEST HOLE
OCTOBER 11, DEVIL TUMOR

03:48.019 --> 03:49.938
THE BEGINNING

03:55.526 --> 03:58.029
That's it. Next is...

04:15.797 --> 04:17.799
Even with treatment,

04:17.882 --> 04:22.220
the human body cannot withstand
the sudden changes caused by magic.

04:22.762 --> 04:26.474
In the end, most patients
die suddenly like that.

04:27.267 --> 04:30.645
Maybe what I'm doing is meaningless.

04:31.354 --> 04:33.731
Or am I just...

04:35.358 --> 04:40.613
This departed soul died from magic, right?
Did you implant the plate properly?

04:42.323 --> 04:45.076
Please take this medicine
after breakfast and dinner.

04:45.576 --> 04:47.620
- All right.
- Take care.

04:47.704 --> 04:50.832
Ai, let's have some lunch soon.

04:52.375 --> 04:56.754
I wonder if this sky
is connected to the magic world?

04:56.838 --> 04:59.173
You miss your wife, don't you?

05:00.341 --> 05:04.804
It's already been a year
since you started helping me, Ai.

05:07.140 --> 05:11.227
After work, what are you always doing,
holed up in the laboratory?

05:11.728 --> 05:14.439
Perhaps you still haven't given up?

05:18.609 --> 05:22.030
Why do you want
to become a Sorcerer so badly?

05:23.573 --> 05:25.533
You asked me that before.

05:26.326 --> 05:28.661
You didn't answer me that time.

05:30.955 --> 05:34.876
We humans in the Hole are all their prey.

05:35.376 --> 05:37.253
Is that what you don't like?

05:37.754 --> 05:42.300
You're helping victims of magic.
That's what keeps you going, isn't it?

05:43.885 --> 05:46.804
That's not the kind of person I am.

05:47.889 --> 05:49.015
I...

05:54.604 --> 05:57.732
I can't find a reason
to live in this town.

05:59.400 --> 06:00.526
We gotta hurry!

06:00.610 --> 06:04.072
The local association
threw the Sorcerer into the waste lake.

06:07.909 --> 06:09.827
He's that far out!

06:12.163 --> 06:18.586
It's a deadly mix of the Hole's sewage,
waste water, and Sorcerers' corpses.

06:19.337 --> 06:21.589
There's no way we can get him out.

06:22.173 --> 06:23.674
Time to give up.

06:24.759 --> 06:25.760
Ai?

06:30.056 --> 06:32.433
Ai! Hang in there!

06:34.936 --> 06:39.357
The lake's water has melted his flesh
and reached his internal organs.

06:40.108 --> 06:41.609
It's already too late.

06:43.861 --> 06:45.863
- Professor...
- Ai!

06:46.447 --> 06:50.201
Please look at my notebook.

06:51.786 --> 06:55.039
Don't tell me you're giving this to me?

06:55.123 --> 06:56.332
Just one more corpse.

06:57.542 --> 07:01.879
If we had one more Sorcerer's corpse,
we could do the surgery.

07:03.047 --> 07:05.633
Listen, please, professor.

07:05.716 --> 07:08.928
If I'm going to die anyway,
make me a Sorcerer,

07:09.011 --> 07:12.432
even if it's just for show.

07:16.936 --> 07:18.271
All right.

07:19.188 --> 07:24.193
If I can turn even a bit of your despair
here in the Hole into hope...

07:33.578 --> 07:35.788
Am I insane?

07:37.707 --> 07:40.918
Doing a make-believe surgery like this...

07:46.007 --> 07:48.050
DAY 1

07:48.134 --> 07:50.178
It's a miracle you survived.

07:50.261 --> 07:54.515
I think we'll still have to do
a few more minor surgeries.

07:54.599 --> 07:58.686
Let me keep a record
of how your body heals.

08:01.189 --> 08:06.569
Did that surgery
really turn him into a Sorcerer?

08:07.111 --> 08:10.615
No, that can't be possible.

08:10.698 --> 08:13.701
There's no way
a human could create a Sorcerer.

08:13.784 --> 08:15.203
DAY 201

08:21.042 --> 08:23.961
KASUKABE'S CLINIC

08:24.879 --> 08:26.464
- Professor.
- Yeah?

08:26.547 --> 08:31.511
I've gotten well enough to walk again,
so today I'd like to try going outside.

08:32.220 --> 08:34.972
Sure. Go take a break and clear your head.

08:39.936 --> 08:44.398
Professor, when I fell into that lake,

08:44.482 --> 08:47.860
that mud and stinking sludge
wrapped around me so heavily,

08:47.944 --> 08:51.948
I felt like I'd become one
with this twisted Hole.

08:52.949 --> 08:58.454
And once I crawled out of there,
I was definitely reborn.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.374
Professor Kasukabe.

09:01.999 --> 09:04.627
I became a Sorcerer.

09:10.550 --> 09:15.596
The next day, Ai's corpse was discovered.

09:16.722 --> 09:17.932
THE PRESENT

09:18.516 --> 09:21.143
Ai's corpse disappeared.

09:21.227 --> 09:25.147
Which means there are
two different possibilities.

09:26.983 --> 09:31.153
Mr. Kasukabe, I looked into
some documents from 13 years ago.

09:31.237 --> 09:35.741
Ai Coleman, plate number 96925.

09:35.825 --> 09:37.159
This number is...

09:39.245 --> 09:44.041
Why do I gotta eat with the people
who dug up my grandson's grave?

09:44.625 --> 09:48.004
The grave was empty anyway,
so what's the big deal?

09:48.087 --> 09:50.798
I'm asking you!
Where the hell did the body go?

09:50.881 --> 09:53.175
Where's my grandson's body?!

09:55.177 --> 09:56.929
- Professor!
- Sorry for the wait!

09:57.430 --> 09:58.931
Where did you go?

09:59.015 --> 10:04.312
I went to the Hole's neighborhood council,
but they hadn't recovered his plate.

10:04.395 --> 10:08.316
The wax figure I saw in that house was Ai.

10:08.399 --> 10:10.318
Say what?! What happened to my grandson?!

10:10.401 --> 10:13.696
Ai. So that's the name of the guy.

10:13.779 --> 10:16.157
Mr. Coleman, you may not be aware,

10:16.240 --> 10:20.328
but I did surgery on Ai
to turn him into a Sorcerer.

10:20.411 --> 10:21.579
What did you say?

10:21.662 --> 10:23.581
Such a noisy old geezer!

10:23.664 --> 10:26.459
So that's what the file was about.

10:26.542 --> 10:31.339
Mr. Coleman. Ai might still be alive
in the world of the Sorcerers.

10:31.422 --> 10:32.548
What did you just--

10:32.632 --> 10:34.050
Shut up a bit!

10:35.259 --> 10:39.722
I plan to return to the Sorcerers' world
and look for Ai.

10:39.805 --> 10:43.059
I don't wanna. I'm definitely not going.

10:43.559 --> 10:45.227
Mr. Kasukabe.

10:45.728 --> 10:49.482
Noi and I are planning to kill
the Cross-Eyes' boss, you know.

10:49.565 --> 10:51.984
Yeah, I know.

10:54.028 --> 10:55.988
Looks like it's going to rain.

10:57.073 --> 10:58.741
Time to go, Noi.

10:58.824 --> 11:00.451
Thanks for the food.

11:00.534 --> 11:02.745
Who's going to pay the bill?

11:04.080 --> 11:05.998
Whoa! A Sorcerer!

11:06.082 --> 11:07.875
Come, Mr. Kasukabe.

11:07.958 --> 11:11.379
But you'd better look out for yourself.

11:11.462 --> 11:13.005
Don't count on me.

11:14.715 --> 11:18.135
Vaux, take care of the bill for me.

11:18.219 --> 11:20.721
I don't think I'll be back for a while.

11:20.805 --> 11:22.139
That's a real help.

11:22.223 --> 11:23.849
We're off.

11:24.350 --> 11:27.645
Mr. Coleman,
I'll let you know if I find Ai.

11:28.229 --> 11:29.146
Jonson?

11:34.610 --> 11:37.029
They were all Sorcerers?!

11:37.113 --> 11:39.240
What is it now?

11:39.323 --> 11:44.245
Because of this neck,
it takes so long to gulp down food!

11:46.372 --> 11:47.832
TRAVEL COMPANIONS

11:47.915 --> 11:49.875
My name is Ebisu.

11:49.959 --> 11:52.753
In the Hole,
I was attacked by a lizard-faced man

11:52.837 --> 11:54.964
and forgot who I really was.

11:55.464 --> 11:59.218
But thanks to En's strange mushrooms,
I remembered my parents

11:59.301 --> 12:01.429
and recalled who I really was.

12:02.138 --> 12:04.598
I can finally go home.

12:04.682 --> 12:07.643
Life at En's house was brutal.

12:07.727 --> 12:10.020
I have no regrets. However...

12:10.104 --> 12:11.063
Crap!

12:13.190 --> 12:16.569
I had some free time,
so I thought I'd see you off.

12:18.863 --> 12:20.573
Hey, say something.

12:20.656 --> 12:23.367
I won't say anything unnecessary.

12:23.451 --> 12:26.787
I'm a calm and silent Sorcerer.

12:26.871 --> 12:28.497
- Idiot.
- Loser.

12:29.790 --> 12:30.875
Wait!

12:31.375 --> 12:36.297
Please refrain from rushing onto the train
as it is extremely dangerous.

12:37.506 --> 12:40.050
You just tried
to use magic on me, didn't you?

12:40.134 --> 12:44.805
I can't go home looking like this.
I have to change my clothes somewhere.

12:45.389 --> 12:47.850
What is she thinking?

12:53.230 --> 12:55.107
Wait, you idiot!

12:57.777 --> 12:58.861
The bathroom?

12:58.944 --> 13:03.616
But I didn't get any good clothes
from En's place.

13:04.450 --> 13:08.537
My parents know me
as a super ordinary, cute girl,

13:08.621 --> 13:11.207
so they'll get mad if I show up like this.

13:11.707 --> 13:16.629
The dress I ordered
got totally ruined thanks to Fujita.

13:16.712 --> 13:18.631
The lingerie doesn't even fit.

13:18.714 --> 13:20.883
The bone dress exposes my underwear.

13:20.966 --> 13:23.886
Fujita's lame outfit
from when I went to the Hole...

13:23.969 --> 13:26.263
Weird uniforms are out of the question.

13:36.857 --> 13:39.360
To hell with the clothes.

13:39.443 --> 13:42.154
I've been missing this entire time.

13:42.238 --> 13:46.033
Mom and Dad will just be happy I'm home.

13:46.116 --> 13:49.703
You took your time.
So, did you have diarrhea again?

13:49.787 --> 13:50.746
I didn't!

13:52.915 --> 13:54.542
I finally got you to talk.

13:58.128 --> 14:00.965
I have to get rid of this guy somehow.

14:01.048 --> 14:03.926
Maybe I should ask
my shady Black Tent pals for help.

14:06.971 --> 14:10.391
It's so loud! This is your house?!

14:10.474 --> 14:13.894
Just like I thought.
Your family's all screwed up.

14:13.978 --> 14:14.937
Hey!

14:15.729 --> 14:18.274
Aren't you Ebisu? It's been a while.

14:19.191 --> 14:21.277
What? Some weirdo's following you?

14:21.360 --> 14:23.362
Then take the back exit.

14:23.445 --> 14:25.281
Oda will show you the way.

14:25.865 --> 14:28.284
I'm Oda. I'll take you to the exit.

14:28.367 --> 14:31.036
Who is this guy?
Never seen his face before.

14:31.704 --> 14:34.456
What is this place? Isn't this your house?

14:35.207 --> 14:36.584
Hey! Wait!

14:37.334 --> 14:39.795
Crap! Hey! Open up!

14:39.879 --> 14:41.714
You're Ebisu, right?

14:41.797 --> 14:45.342
Got any of that black powder?
It's been hard to find lately.

14:46.010 --> 14:47.344
Black powder...

14:48.429 --> 14:51.765
So you won't talk
to a newbie like me, is that it?

14:51.849 --> 14:53.183
That's right.

14:58.314 --> 15:00.733
I'm back home!

15:03.819 --> 15:06.196
Dad and Mom will probably be surprised.

15:06.280 --> 15:07.615
Coming!

15:08.782 --> 15:10.200
Can I help you?

15:12.620 --> 15:14.455
Who are you?

15:14.538 --> 15:16.957
My name is Ebisu.

15:18.751 --> 15:22.796
You're lying. That's not true!
I'm Ebisu, you fool!

15:23.297 --> 15:24.924
Dad! Mom!

15:32.348 --> 15:33.641
They're not here.

15:34.141 --> 15:36.143
Dad and Mom aren't here.

15:36.226 --> 15:39.396
They went to work and never came back.

15:41.231 --> 15:42.650
Who are you?

15:42.733 --> 15:46.904
I'm Ebisu, the daughter of this family!
Who the heck are you?

15:49.657 --> 15:51.492
I'm also Ebisu.

15:51.992 --> 15:55.579
You have the same face as me?

15:56.997 --> 15:58.499
A doppelgänger!

16:03.629 --> 16:04.922
Wait!

16:14.515 --> 16:17.393
It's okay, she left.

16:17.476 --> 16:18.644
Nanny!

16:18.727 --> 16:21.897
My lady. You're really alive.

16:21.981 --> 16:23.899
Nanny!

16:23.983 --> 16:27.861
My lady. You're really my lady.

16:27.945 --> 16:29.154
Where are Dad and Mom?

16:29.238 --> 16:32.491
Ever since you went missing, my lady,

16:32.574 --> 16:35.911
your parents have been heartbroken.

16:36.537 --> 16:42.292
At that time, your father invited
a shady Sorcerer to the mansion.

16:42.376 --> 16:47.047
My magic is so advanced,
it shortens my life every time I use it.

16:47.131 --> 16:49.800
Because of that, it's expensive.
Are you sure?

16:49.883 --> 16:53.303
I'll pay anything.
Please save our daughter.

16:53.387 --> 16:55.556
This is our daughter's hair.

16:55.639 --> 17:00.310
All right, then.
Now, put that hair into my forehead.

17:02.146 --> 17:03.689
Okay!

17:15.534 --> 17:18.454
Now, open the cap
and squeeze out what's inside!

17:18.537 --> 17:19.830
- Yes!
- Yes!

17:25.919 --> 17:27.838
Now, keep it coming!!

17:56.992 --> 17:59.536
That's what came out.

17:59.620 --> 18:03.540
At the beginning,
the master treated her with affection.

18:03.624 --> 18:06.543
On the outside, she's identical to you,

18:06.627 --> 18:09.421
but inside, she's something else entirely.

18:09.505 --> 18:14.843
Out of fear, the master and mistress
abandoned the estate and ran away.

18:17.721 --> 18:19.848
Nanny! You burnt the cookies.

18:19.932 --> 18:22.392
You burnt my precious cookies.

18:22.476 --> 18:24.144
You're fired now.

18:26.438 --> 18:28.857
You have the same face as me.

18:29.733 --> 18:34.488
I get it. You're a fake me.

18:43.413 --> 18:45.457
I'll be killed at this rate!

19:12.818 --> 19:14.486
Two bags left.

19:39.845 --> 19:43.265
Hey, three more meals!

19:43.348 --> 19:45.767
There are so many customers today.

19:45.851 --> 19:49.855
Come on, work harder, part-timers!

19:50.355 --> 19:52.691
Damn her for making us work like dogs.

19:52.774 --> 19:53.984
Deal with it.

19:54.067 --> 19:57.613
Even if we don't pay the rent,
we still gotta feed five people.

19:58.113 --> 20:00.574
It looks delicious.

20:00.657 --> 20:03.035
What a cruel job this is.

20:03.118 --> 20:06.079
The boss will be back soon.
Have a little patience.

20:06.163 --> 20:08.290
What the hell are you snacking on?

20:08.373 --> 20:10.292
MAGMA BATH

20:15.255 --> 20:19.426
I was friends with Risu
and a student at that school.

20:19.509 --> 20:21.929
He knows my true identity.

20:23.805 --> 20:26.642
But what is this anxiety I feel?

20:29.811 --> 20:32.314
I hope I get to see the boss.

20:32.397 --> 20:34.524
What's the boss like?

20:34.608 --> 20:36.735
Really strong.

20:36.818 --> 20:40.447
He's a savior to those like us
who can't use magic.

20:41.740 --> 20:44.910
I want to be the boss's girl.

20:44.993 --> 20:47.162
Big Bro's hard to pass up, though.

20:50.874 --> 20:52.000
Strange clothes.

20:52.084 --> 20:55.212
I just got the cross tattoo,
and it stings like crazy.

20:55.837 --> 20:57.714
I brought you your food.

20:57.798 --> 20:59.967
Looks delicious!

21:00.592 --> 21:02.344
Local sake, on the house.

21:07.349 --> 21:08.976
Guess I'm seeing things.

21:09.059 --> 21:11.478
Big Bro, one more!

21:15.440 --> 21:17.484
You both are drinking too much.

21:17.567 --> 21:19.820
It's fine. Nikaido, you drink too.

21:19.903 --> 21:23.323
This tiny sushi is delicious.

21:23.407 --> 21:27.077
It looks like Caiman has cheered up
thanks to the sake and food.

21:27.160 --> 21:28.578
I'm glad.

21:28.662 --> 21:30.747
Big Bro, I like you. Kiss!

21:30.831 --> 21:32.332
Whoa!

21:34.584 --> 21:39.506
Natsuki hasn't noticed that the crosses
on Caiman's eyes have disappeared?

21:47.389 --> 21:49.016
What's wrong, Nikaido?

21:49.683 --> 21:51.518
Drink one more with me.

21:52.894 --> 21:54.021
Sure.

21:57.149 --> 22:00.485
You've acted weird since we went
to that abandoned school,

22:00.569 --> 22:02.029
so I was worried.

22:02.112 --> 22:04.865
Sorry to worry you.

22:04.948 --> 22:06.033
Say, Caiman.

22:06.116 --> 22:08.744
If you ever got all your memories back,

22:08.827 --> 22:12.748
would you still live in this world
as a Cross-Eye

22:12.831 --> 22:14.791
with Natsuki and the others?

22:14.875 --> 22:18.295
Well, I'm not sure about that.

22:18.378 --> 22:21.882
At least for now,
I'm planning to head back to the Hole.

22:22.382 --> 22:24.551
Why are you even asking that?

22:25.218 --> 22:30.307
Caiman, there's something
I wanted to ask you this entire time.

22:31.016 --> 22:35.812
When you're back to normal,
would you help me out at my restaurant?

22:35.896 --> 22:36.813
What?

22:36.897 --> 22:41.568
Honestly, I was planning to tell you
once all your problems were sorted out.

22:42.069 --> 22:46.990
But, for some reason,
I feel like I have to ask you now.

22:47.074 --> 22:49.409
Would you be okay with someone like me?

22:52.412 --> 22:55.332
Yeah. I could use your help, Caiman.

22:56.583 --> 22:57.834
Nikaido.

22:58.418 --> 23:01.588
I'll go out of business
if you just stay a customer.

23:01.671 --> 23:02.506
Awesome!

23:04.216 --> 23:06.510
My prediction was correct.

23:07.344 --> 23:14.226
After all, that night was the last time
I ever talked to Caiman.

24:43.148 --> 24:44.941
THE END

24:45.025 --> 24:47.235
What we learned in Episode 5.

24:47.319 --> 24:48.987
That man's name is Ai.

24:49.070 --> 24:50.947
Ebisu comes from a respectable family.

24:51.031 --> 24:53.575
Caiman and Nikaido have a nice vibe.

24:53.658 --> 24:57.412
What we'll learn in Episode 6
is still hidden in chaos.

24:57.496 --> 24:59.956
This is Dorohedoro.
